---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SEOHead from '../components/SEOHead.astro';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <SEOHead
    slot="head"
    title="Jacob Steelsmith | Cloud Platform Engineer"
    description="Cloud platform engineer specializing in AWS, serverless architectures, distributed systems, and technical leadership. Building scalable infrastructure with Infrastructure-as-Code."
    ogType="website"
  />

  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
    <h1 id="hero-heading">Jacob Steelsmith</h1>
    <p class="hero-subtitle">AI Systems & Cloud Architect | AWS Serverless | Distributed Systems | Engineering Leadership</p>
    <p class="hero-intro">
      Hands-on software engineer and engineering leader with 20+ years of experience architecting and operating scalable cloud, data, and distributed systems. My background spans agentic AI development, AWS serverless architecture, platform modernization, and full-stack application development, with a focus on building reliable systems that support real-world operational workflows at scale.
    </p>
    <p class="hero-intro">
      My experience spans monolithic and cloud-native architectures, including designing and building transactional platforms, APIs, and operational systems used by thousands of users. I've led the evolution of legacy applications into scalable distributed systems, while continuing to contribute directly to implementation, debugging, and system design.
    </p>
    <p class="hero-intro">
      While I've taken on leadership responsibilities, I'm at my best when working closely with the code and the systems themselves. I've owned production environments, including performance, reliability, and incident response, and focus on building maintainable systems that perform under real-world conditions.
    </p>
    <p class="hero-intro">
      I use modern tools, including AI-assisted development, to accelerate delivery, improve code quality, and better understand complex systems, but always grounded in strong engineering fundamentals.
    </p>
    <p class="hero-intro">
      I'm particularly interested in roles where I can contribute as a senior engineer or hands-on leader, helping teams build, scale, and operate reliable systems.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="highlights" aria-labelledby="highlights-heading">
    <h2 id="highlights-heading">What I Do</h2>
    <ul class="highlights-grid" role="list">
      <li class="highlight-card">
        <h3>AWS Cloud Architecture</h3>
        <p>
          Deep expertise across the AWS ecosystem including compute, storage, networking, and managed services.
          Designing solutions that balance performance, cost, and operational simplicity.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="highlight-card">
        <h3>Serverless &amp; Distributed Systems</h3>
        <p>
          Building event-driven architectures with Lambda, Step Functions, EventBridge, and SQS.
          Designing systems that scale automatically and handle failure gracefully.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="highlight-card">
        <h3>Infrastructure as Code</h3>
        <p>
          Defining reproducible infrastructure with CloudFormation and Terraform. Automating deployments
          through CI/CD pipelines with OIDC authentication and least-privilege access.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="highlight-card">
        <h3>Technical Leadership</h3>
        <p>
          Guiding engineering teams through architecture decisions, code reviews, and best practices.
          Mentoring developers and establishing standards that improve delivery velocity and system reliability.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="cta" aria-labelledby="cta-heading">
    <h2 id="cta-heading">Learn More</h2>
    <p>
      Explore my <a href="/resume/">resume</a> for a detailed look at my experience,
      check out my <a href="/projects/">projects</a> to see what I've built,
      or review the <a href="https://jacob.steelsmith.org/architecture/">architecture</a> of this site itself as a demonstration of AWS engineering.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .hero-subtitle {
    font-size: var(--font-size-xl);
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .hero-intro {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .highlights {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .highlights h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .highlights-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .highlight-card {
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background-color: var(--color-bg-alt);
  }

  .highlight-card h3 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xl);
  }

  .highlight-card p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
  }

  .cta {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .cta h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .cta p {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .highlights-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
